>> title: Miso Tare
>> category: Sauces & Gravies
>> tags: japanese, miso, ramen, seasoning, make-ahead
>> counters: Ramen Shop
>> aka: miso tare, 味噌ダレ, miso dare, miso base for ramen, Sapporo miso base, ramen miso paste, miso ramen seasoning
>> pairs-with: miso-ramen
>> servings: 6
>> time: 8 hr 20 min
>> slack: forgiving — the miso is stirred in off the heat; boiled in the pan it loses its aroma entirely and cannot be given it back

>> step: Thicker than the other two tares, and it goes into the wok rather than the bowl.
Thicker than the other two tares, and it goes into the wok rather than the bowl.

>> step: fry the aromatics 2 min
Fry @garlic{4%cloves}(grated), @fresh ginger{1%Tbs}(grated) and @doubanjiang{1%tsp}(fermented broad bean paste) in @toasted sesame oil{2%Tbs}(30 mL) over low heat ~fry{2%min}, until it smells sweet rather than raw and nothing has taken colour.

>> step: boil down by half 3 min
Boil @sake{1/4%cup}(60 mL) and @mirin{2%Tbs}(30 mL) in a small #saucepan{} ~boil{3%min}, down by half.

>> step: beat the miso in off the heat
Beat @white miso{1/2%cup}(140 g), @red miso{1/4%cup}(70 g), @sesame paste{2%Tbs}(35 g; Japanese neri goma or tahini) and @granulated sugar{1%Tbs}(12 g) into @&(~1)reduced sake{} and @&(~2)fried aromatics{} off the heat, until it is a smooth paste that falls slowly off a spoon.

>> step: rest overnight
Rest @&(~1)tare{} in a jar in the fridge ~rest{8%hr} before using.
